WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:07.879
So the other day I was just surfing YouTube
listening to some nostalgic tunes, and I come

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:11.179
upon a video containing the Wii Menu Music.

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:15.619
Now for whatever reason I decided to scroll
down into the comments to see what people

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:21.940
had to say about the music, but I ended noticing
some really weird and kind of disturbing comments

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.142
so I thought I would share them with you in
this video.

00:00:24.142 --> 00:00:27.630
So this person says, "Am I the only one that
finds this soothing?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.539
Like hypnotic?"

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.660
And I was think, yes, it's soothing, but hypnotic?

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.940
I'm not really so sure about that.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.660
But to my surprise I looked at the replies
to the comment and there were quite a few

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.120
people who agreed with him and said, "Same."

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.160
Then there's somebody else that claims sometimes
I just randomly hear this.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.980
And again, there were quite a few people who
experienced the same thing.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.780
One of which said, "IT JUST MELTS INTO YOUR
MIND, CONSUMING IT.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.440
WII MENU IS LOVE.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.329
WII MENU IS LIFE."

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:05.309
So I found it kind of strange that people
were agreeing with these weird comments and

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:06.309
then I see this.

00:01:06.309 --> 00:01:10.450
"I hear it if it's pitch quiet at night, except
for the dishwasher.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:15.829
For some reason, my brain interprets the dishwasher
sounds as this music."

00:01:15.829 --> 00:01:21.310
So I thought surely that nobody else would
agree with that one, but I was wrong because

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.361
this person chimes in: "Same."

00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:28.659
And I just find it strange that something
that specific would be shared by multiple

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:29.659
people.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:33.999
"That song ends up playing when you randomly
wake up at 2AM and this is the song that you

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:35.499
hallucinate hearing."

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:37.719
"My Wii turns on by itself.

00:01:37.719 --> 00:01:40.329
Can anyone tell me why?

00:01:40.329 --> 00:01:42.709
(2 hours later) Wait a second...

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:45.109
Isn't my Wii dead?

00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:48.689
OMG IT'S THE WII SPIRIT IS POSSESSING IT'S
BODY!"

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:51.039
OK can somebody-- what's going on??

00:01:51.039 --> 00:01:52.039
What's the deal with this?

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:55.460
"Sometimes when I'm not near the Wii I just
randomly hear this music."

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.819
"Oh yeah, me too bro."

00:01:56.819 --> 00:01:58.459
"I'm crying.

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:01.420
I can hear the little clicks right now.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.429
You all know what I'm talking about."

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:06.509
"You can make a religion out of this."

00:02:06.509 --> 00:02:10.350
Yeah of course the person with a Pokemon profile
picture would be talking about making a religion

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.800
out of the frickin' Wii music.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.350
"I've had this stuck in my head for the last
24 hours.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.350
HELP."

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:21.140
The weird thing about this is while this music
is soothing or whatever, it isn't like the

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.970
catchiest or poppiest of music.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.049
It's not something I would really find getting
stuck in my head.

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:29.730
I mean, I can think of worse things to have
stuck in your head for 24 hours, but that's

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.690
an insanely long amount of time.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:36.859
"Scientists believe that this sound is that
last thing a human being hears at the point

00:02:36.859 --> 00:02:37.859
of death.

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:40.209
Could this be God himself?"

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:43.349
Maybe this guy should join the Pokemon guy's
religion...

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:45.910
OK, this one's just ridiculous, this one's
off the charts.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.090
"The song is very depressing for me.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.920
Some awful memories and incidents happened
when this music played back in 2007."

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.069
Well, first of all, them me stop you there.

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:00.629
I don't know what happened to this person
but if there are awful things happening around

00:03:00.629 --> 00:03:05.069
you and these scarring incidents are taking
place... why do you still have the Wii on?

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:09.450
And furthermore, if someone's using the Wii,
why would they leave it on the menu thing.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:13.560
In my experience, you boot it up, you hear
this music for less than a minute while you

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.170
choose which game you want to play.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:20.620
"I even have the dates of those things marked
in my Wii Calendar, and it still makes me

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.030
sad for a bit.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.280
For some reason, I still like it."

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.280
Like...

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.280
WHAT?

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.280
First of all, who uses the Wii Calendar?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.689
I can only imagine.

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:29.689
'Yeah.

00:03:29.689 --> 00:03:30.689
Uhm.

00:03:30.689 --> 00:03:32.340
Dad came home drunk again and killed Mom...

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:38.109
I'm gonna go mark this in my Wii Calendar...."

00:03:38.109 --> 00:03:41.300
Again I have no idea what happened to this
person, hopefully it's nothing too bad.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.889
This freaking song drives me insane.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.959
I have no idea why."

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.269
Yeah.. neither do I.

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:49.620
No!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:59.060
No, no, that's impossible!

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:10.859
No, I left you behind!

00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:17.940
We were finished!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:25.020
I moved on!

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:34.750
I bought the Nintendo Switch for $299.99!

